MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Otis Redding collection feels like a natural next choice because its expressive soul singing connects with the warmth and feeling I enjoy in blues and roots rock.",
    "Abbey Road partly fits my interest in melodic classic rock, although Otis Redding is the only record I would choose this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Rust In Peace, Aenima, and Ten offer heavier sounds than I want today; sharing a broad rock connection with Hendrix does not give them the bluesy feel I am seeking.",
    "A Farewell to Kings and the Pink Floyd collection lean toward elaborate or atmospheric rock, while 25, Late Registration, and Hamilton take me further from my current blues and roots-rock mood."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat an interest in rock as a reason to offer heavy, progressive, and grunge records interchangeably.",
    "The list feels too focused on widely recognized albums without enough connection to what drew me to my recent selections."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choices of Old Sock, People, Hell & Angels, and Memphis point toward blues feeling, soulful performances, and roots-oriented music.",
    "I rarely choose anything unless it closely fits what I want, so a loose connection through rock music is not enough to make me pick another record today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in classic music with soul, but stretched it too broadly beyond the blues and roots-rock feeling I want today."
}
